<<~ ahu slot=`#/u1-threat-sketch-a-face-s-session-reaches-the-se`>>

! u1 threat sketch — a face's session reaches the sealed store (2026-10-31)

| authority input | source | what proves it | where the law lives | fails closed to |h
| which session signs | the UDS seat's booking: request id + verb → that socket's signer, for the call's life | the owner's SessionTable, asked by the signer before and after every signature | `session-sign-door.ts` (book), `SessionSigner.sign` | `signer-unavailable` (no booking / other verb / summons) |
| the signature | the session's own SessionSigner on the main thread | its table check; secret never leaves the object | `session-signer.ts` | `signer-refused` (dropped by lock/close/switch) |
| anchor | the supply's anchor (nexus / place) | the session door's proof at that anchor | book: `session-anchor-place` | place sessions reach no sealed verb |
| the face | the booking's proof subject (main), never `invocation.face` | equals faceProofSubjectRef(own chain scope) | island `sessionOf` | `session-face-foreign` |
| the chain (who may write) | the dial presentation's VesselFaceCertificate (scope, vesselFaceKey), public | composed only when the dial's presentation composed at the pin | `dialAnchorCell().chain`, island `ownChainStanding` | holdsWrite false: cert not under the vessel's own chain, or bag not in registerBags |
| ask origin | `context.local` (vessel's own channel) + main's booking | the dispatcher's local-ask book; main books only session calls | island + book | summons refuses (content fence / signer-unavailable) |

Exempt by name: `sealed-memory-*` (vessel-key-signed asks, the house's own; import takes a session signer only where one booked), `sealed-rolls` (vessel receipts).
OPEN (fork F7): seat rolls carry no session → removal rolls stay owed while seals continue under the old version.
Browser: waits for U4 (F6 slice four); route table stays total.

